## ascii Service

The ASCII art rendering engine responsible for converting positioned Mermaid graphs into multi-line strings using box-drawing characters, Unicode shapes, and ANSI color codes.

### Architecture

```mermaid
---
config:
  layout: elk
---
flowchart TB
  subgraph API["Entry Point"]
    AsciiIndex["ascii/index.ts\nrenderMermaidASCII()\ndetectDiagramType()"]
  end

  subgraph Service["Core Rendering"]
    Converter["ascii/converter.ts\nconvertToAsciiGraph()\nconvertSubgraph()"]
    EdgeRouting["ascii/edge-routing.ts\ndetermineDirection()\ndeterminePath()\ndetermineStartAndEndDir()"]
    EdgeBundling["ascii/edge-bundling.ts\nbundle edges"]
    Pathfinder["ascii/pathfinder.ts\npath finding"]
    Grid["ascii/grid.ts\ngridToDrawingCoord()\nreserveSpotInGrid()\nsetColumnWidth()"]
    Canvas["ascii/canvas.ts\nmkCanvas()\ncopyCanvas()\nmkRoleCanvas()"]
    MultilineUtils["ascii/multiline-utils.ts\nmeasure/wrap labels"]
  end

  subgraph DiagramRenderers["Diagram-Specific Renderers"]
    ClassDiagram["ascii/class-diagram.ts\nbuildClassSections()\nformatMember()\ngetRelMarker()"]
    ErDiagram["ascii/er-diagram.ts\nbuildEntitySections()\nformatAttribute()\ngetCrowsFootChars()"]
    Sequence["ascii/sequence.ts\nrenderSequenceAscii()"]
  end

  subgraph Data["Types & Validation"]
    Types["ascii/types.ts\nAsciiNode / AsciiEdge / AsciiGraph\nAsciiConfig / Canvas / GridCoord\nDrawingCoord / Direction / CharRole"]
    Ansi["ascii/ansi.ts\ndiagramColorsToAsciiTheme()\ndetectColorMode()\nmixColors()"]
    Validate["ascii/validate.ts\nhasDiagonalLines()\nassertNoDiagonals()"]
    ShapesLib["ascii/shapes/\nShapeRegistry\nrender() per shape type"]
  end

  AsciiIndex --> Converter
  AsciiIndex --> ClassDiagram
  AsciiIndex --> ErDiagram
  AsciiIndex --> Sequence
  Converter --> EdgeRouting
  Converter --> Grid
  EdgeRouting --> Pathfinder
  EdgeRouting --> Grid
  Grid --> Canvas
  AsciiIndex --> ShapesLib
  AsciiIndex --> Ansi
  Validate --> Types
  ClassDiagram --> Types
  ErDiagram --> Types
  Sequence --> Types
```

### Architectural Layers

**Service Layer** (all logic — no data/API/external layers):
- **Entry**: `ascii/index.ts` exports `renderMermaidASCII()` and `AsciiRenderOptions`. Detects diagram type and dispatches to the appropriate pipeline.
- **Conversion**: `converter.ts` transforms a `MermaidGraph` (from the main parser) into an `AsciiGraph` with grid coordinates and subgraph structure.
- **Grid & Routing**: `grid.ts` manages a 2D coordinate space. `edge-routing.ts` computes direction, start/end points, and full paths for each edge. `pathfinder.ts` performs A*-style path-finding around obstacles.
- **Canvas**: `canvas.ts` provides a 2D character buffer (`Canvas` type) with copy/resize operations. Each node and edge is rendered into canvas regions.
- **Diagram Renderers**: `class-diagram.ts`, `er-diagram.ts`, and `sequence.ts` provide diagram-type-specific rendering logic on top of the generic engine.
- **Theme/Color**: `ansi.ts` converts `DiagramColors` into ASCII-specific theme tokens and detects dark/light terminal color mode.
- **Validation**: `validate.ts` detects and asserts the absence of diagonal line artifacts in ASCII output.

### Technology Stack

| Technology | Version | Role |
|---|---|---|
| TypeScript | — | Implementation language |
| Bun | — | Runtime & test runner |

### Architecture Violations

None detected.

