## shapes Service

The shape renderer library used by the ASCII engine. Each file exports a `ShapeRenderer` implementing `getDimensions()`, `render()`, and `getAttachmentPoint()`.

### Architecture

```mermaid
---
config:
  layout: elk
---
flowchart TB
  subgraph API["Shape Registry"]
    Index["shapes/index.ts\nShapeRegistry\ngetShapeRenderer(shape)"]
  end

  subgraph Service["Shape Implementations"]
    Rectangle["shapes/rectangle.ts\ngetBoxDimensions()\nrenderBox()\ngetBoxAttachmentPoint()"]
    Circle["shapes/circle.ts\nrender() — calls getCorners('circle')"]
    Diamond["shapes/diamond.ts\nrender() — rotated square"]
    Hexagon["shapes/hexagon.ts\nrender() — calls getCorners('hexagon')"]
    Rounded["shapes/rounded.ts\nrender() — rounded rect"]
    Stadium["shapes/stadium.ts\nrender() — pill shape"]
    Special["shapes/special.ts\nrender() — asymmetric shapes"]
    State["shapes/state.ts\nStartState.render()\nEndState.render()"]
    Corners["shapes/corners.ts\ngetCorners(shape, useAscii)\ncorner char tables"]
  end

  subgraph Data["Types"]
    Types["shapes/types.ts\nShapeRenderer (interface)\nShapeDimensions (interface)\nShapeRenderOptions (interface)\nShapeRegistry (type)"]
  end

  Index --> Rectangle
  Index --> Circle
  Index --> Diamond
  Index --> Hexagon
  Index --> Rounded
  Index --> Stadium
  Index --> Special
  Index --> State
  Circle --> Corners
  Hexagon --> Corners
  Rounded --> Corners
  Stadium --> Corners
  Circle --> Rectangle
  Diamond --> Rectangle
  Hexagon --> Rectangle
  State --> Types
  Index --> Types
```

### Architectural Layers

**Service Layer** (all logic):
- **Registry**: `shapes/index.ts` maps `AsciiNodeShape` values to `ShapeRenderer` instances.
- **Base Shape**: `rectangle.ts` provides the foundational `renderBox()` and `getBoxAttachmentPoint()` functions used by most other shapes.
- **Composite Shapes**: `circle.ts`, `hexagon.ts`, `stadium.ts`, and `rounded.ts` build on `rectangle.ts` + `corners.ts` for rounded/curved variants.
- **Specialized**: `diamond.ts` renders rotated squares; `special.ts` handles asymmetric shapes; `state.ts` renders start/end state nodes.
- **Corners**: `corners.ts` provides corner character lookup tables for both Unicode box-drawing and plain ASCII fallback modes.

### Technology Stack

| Technology | Role |
|---|---|
| TypeScript | Implementation language |

### Architecture Violations

None detected.

