  Index --> ClassParser
  Index --> ClassLayout
  Index --> ClassRenderer
  Index --> ErParser
  Index --> ErLayout
  Index --> ErRenderer
  Index --> SeqParser
  Index --> SeqLayout
  Index --> SeqRenderer
  Layout --> ElkInstance
  ClassLayout --> ElkInstance
  ErLayout --> ElkInstance
  ElkInstance --> ELK
  Index --> Entities
  Renderer --> Theme
  Renderer --> MultilineUtils
  Renderer --> ShapeClipping
  ClassRenderer --> Theme
  ClassRenderer --> MultilineUtils
  ErRenderer --> Theme
  ErRenderer --> MultilineUtils
  SeqRenderer --> Theme
  SeqRenderer --> MultilineUtils
  MultilineUtils --> TextMetrics
```

### Architectural Layers

**Service Layer** (all logic — no HTTP API or database layers):

- **Public API** (`src/index.ts`): Single entry point. Decodes XML entities, detects diagram type, dispatches to the correct parse → layout → render pipeline, and returns an SVG string. Exports both sync and async variants plus the ASCII entry point.

- **Parsers**:
  - `src/parser.ts` — `parseMermaid()` handles flowchart/state diagrams. Parses node definitions, edge connections, subgraphs, and style classes into `MermaidGraph`.
  - `src/class/parser.ts` — `parseClassDiagram()` parses class member syntax (attributes, methods) and relationship lines into `ClassDiagram`.
  - `src/er/parser.ts` — `parseErDiagram()` parses entity definitions, attributes, and relationship cardinalities.
  - `src/sequence/parser.ts` — `parseSequenceDiagram()` parses actors, messages, activations, notes, and loops.

- **Layout**:
  - `src/layout.ts` — `layoutGraphSync()` orchestrates ELK layout for flowcharts. Handles node sizing (multiline labels), edge routing points, and subgraph nesting.
  - `src/class/layout.ts` — `layoutClassDiagramSync()` positions class nodes with ELK, accounting for member list heights.
  - `src/er/layout.ts` — `layoutErDiagramSync()` positions entity boxes with ELK.
  - `src/sequence/layout.ts` — `layoutSequenceDiagram()` uses a custom top-down layout (no ELK): computes actor column widths, message rows, activation boxes, and lifeline spans.

- **SVG Renderers**:
  - `src/renderer.ts` — `renderSvg()` generates SVG for flowcharts with `<g>` groups, `<path>` edges, arrow markers, and node shapes.
  - `src/class/renderer.ts` — `renderClassSvg()` renders class boxes with sections (name, attributes, methods) and relationship lines.
  - `src/er/renderer.ts` — `renderErSvg()` renders entity boxes with attribute rows (syntax-highlighted with monospace spans) and crow's foot relationship edges.
  - `src/sequence/renderer.ts` — `renderSequenceSvg()` renders actor boxes/stick-figures, lifelines, activation boxes, messages with arrows, notes, and loop/group frames.

- **Theme System** (`src/theme.ts`): Defines `DiagramColors` (bg, fg, line, accent, muted, surface, border). Provides named themes (`THEMES`), defaults (`DEFAULTS`), and `fromShikiTheme()` to map Shiki syntax-highlight colors to diagram colors. `buildStyleBlock()` generates a `<style>` block with CSS custom properties and optional Google Fonts. `svgOpenTag()` embeds colors as inline CSS vars on the `<svg>` element.

- **Utilities**:
  - `multiline-utils.ts` — Normalizes Mermaid `<br>` labels, parses inline formatting (`<b>`, `<i>`, `<s>`, `<u>`), renders multi-line `<tspan>` blocks with optional background rectangles.
  - `text-metrics.ts` — Measures text width and height without a DOM using character width tables.
  - `styles.ts` — Processes Mermaid `classDef` and `style` directives.
  - `shape-clipping.ts` — Computes edge endpoint coordinates clipped to node boundaries.
  - `elk-instance.ts` — Manages the ELK singleton with a `FakeWorker` bypass for synchronous layout.
  - `browser.ts` — Provides ambient browser global declarations for non-DOM environments.

### Technology Stack

| Technology | Version | Role |
|---|---|---|
| TypeScript | — | Implementation language |
| Bun | — | Runtime, test runner (`bun test`) |
| elkjs | ^0.11.0 | Graph layout engine (flowchart, class, ER) |
| entities | ^7.0.1 | XML entity decoding |
| shiki | ^3.19.0 (devDep) | Optional theme integration |

### Architecture Violations

